# | ENTES MPR-53S Network Analyser (Modbus RTU RS-485)
# | 
# | Source: entes-mpr-53s-register-table-tr.pdf (A4308/Rev.2)
# | Protocol: Modbus RTU; FC03 read, FC06 write single register
# | All addresses are 0-based decimal. All registers are 16-bit (1 word each).
# | 
# | Multipliers:
# | Voltage:        raw × 0.1  = V   (incorporates VT ratio)
# | Current:        raw × 0.001 = A  (incorporates CT ratio)
# | Active/reactive power: raw × 0.1 = W/VAr (signed for per-phase)
# | Apparent power: raw × 0.1  = VA
# | Power factor:   raw × 0.001 = dimensionless (−1.000..1.000, signed)
# | Frequency:      raw × 0.01 = Hz
# | Angle:          raw × 1    = degree
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Entes
@model=MPR-53S
@description=3-phase network analyser, Modbus RTU, 16-bit registers. Phase-neutral voltages at addr 0-4 (V×0.1); phase currents at 6-12 (A×0.001); phase-phase voltages at 14-18; per-phase active/reactive/apparent power at 20-36 (W/VAr/VA×0.1); per-phase cos-phi at 38-42 (×0.001); total import/export active, inductive/capacitive reactive, apparent at 44-52; avg cos-phi at 54-56; frequency at 58 (Hz×0.01); voltage/current angles at 60-70 (deg); THD at 72-82 (×0.1%); digital input at 84; dual-tariff 64-bit energy counters at 86-116; min at 118-162; max at 164-208; current demand at 210-214; per-phase and total max demand at 216-254. Settings at 0x8000: VT/CT ratio, calc method, demand time, pulse, energy counter, comms.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/entes-mpr-53s.toml; Source: entes-mpr-53s-register-table-tr.pdf (A4308/Rev.2). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
